WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.805 --> 01:30.705
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.624 --> 01:33.959
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.835 --> 01:35.878
Black Jack.

01:48.933 --> 01:52.060
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "Move, Solomon”

01:48.933 --> 01:52.060
Move, Solomon

01:58.353 --> 01:59.353
Hey!

01:59.793 --> 02:02.433
Pinoco-chan, hurry!

02:05.765 --> 02:09.562
Remember, you can't swim, so never get in the water!

02:15.024 --> 02:18.568
I have the tube, so I should be fine.

02:18.569 --> 02:20.278
Here I come!

02:23.366 --> 02:24.199
Pinoco...

02:26.661 --> 02:27.744
Pinoco-chan!

02:28.496 --> 02:29.704
Pinoco-chan!

02:44.053 --> 02:46.596
Pinoco-chan!

02:47.014 --> 02:48.528
She's not coming back up.

02:48.575 --> 02:49.349
She's drowning.

03:00.152 --> 03:00.986
Are you okay?

03:01.112 --> 03:01.695
Hey!

03:04.949 --> 03:06.116
Excuse me.

03:06.117 --> 03:07.450
Please let me through!

03:07.451 --> 03:08.535
Excuse me!

03:20.506 --> 03:21.298
No good...

03:50.328 --> 03:51.911
You're breathing again.

03:54.332 --> 03:55.332
More.

04:00.421 --> 04:01.379
Are you okay?

04:01.380 --> 04:02.172
Yup.

04:02.173 --> 04:04.507
You are nice to the ladies.

04:04.508 --> 04:06.760
Thank you so much.

04:07.053 --> 04:09.349
I only did what had to be done.

04:09.889 --> 04:13.767
I work here part-time as a lifeguard.

04:15.227 --> 04:17.312
Swimming is your job?

04:17.480 --> 04:20.148
No wonder you're so good at swimming.

04:20.149 --> 04:22.932
No, no, being a lifeguard is my side job.

04:23.402 --> 04:25.487
My real job is an animator.

04:26.155 --> 04:26.905
Ani...

04:27.031 --> 04:28.365
mator?!

04:29.241 --> 04:30.450
What's that?

04:36.582 --> 04:38.833
You see these two pictures?

04:41.420 --> 04:43.964
Put them like this...

04:46.634 --> 04:47.926
It's moving!

04:47.927 --> 04:49.886
It's the basis of animation.

04:50.262 --> 04:51.680
That's amazing!

04:53.641 --> 04:55.892
But your room is messy.

04:56.936 --> 04:58.520
Pinoco-chan!

05:00.356 --> 05:02.233
This desk is strange.

05:02.346 --> 05:04.484
There's glass on top.

05:04.485 --> 05:06.242
This is a desk for anime.

05:06.570 --> 05:10.156
l light it up like this, and trace the pictures.

05:10.533 --> 05:11.578
Why?

05:11.826 --> 05:14.661
I lay another sheet of paper over the one with a picture,

05:15.663 --> 05:17.872
and draw something that's just a little different.

05:21.043 --> 05:24.916
And after I draw more pictures...

05:27.300 --> 05:27.909
See?

05:29.010 --> 05:31.094
The lion started moving!

05:31.177 --> 05:33.556
Poster: Roar, Solomon!

05:31.637 --> 05:33.359
Those who draw these are animators.

05:33.764 --> 05:36.266
And that's my job.

05:37.018 --> 05:38.890
When these pictures are drawn well,

05:39.186 --> 05:41.438
the pictures start moving as if they were given life.

05:49.905 --> 05:52.032
Anime must be alive!

05:53.075 --> 05:57.203
We are the engineers who give life to images!

05:57.538 --> 05:59.205
So cool!

05:59.624 --> 06:01.499
Doing the usual, Musashi?

06:03.878 --> 06:04.808
Kojiro-kun!

06:05.129 --> 06:07.255
The famous Kojiro?

06:08.966 --> 06:11.801
He's a very well-known director in the field of anime.

06:12.803 --> 06:14.874
Everything he works on becomes a huge hit.

06:15.181 --> 06:17.766
I think he was once an animator.

06:19.185 --> 06:21.478
You were like that ever since you were in high school.

06:22.021 --> 06:24.314
Why don't you stop dreaming,

06:24.899 --> 06:27.567
and look at reality?

06:28.235 --> 06:30.487
I have no intention of changing myself.

06:32.573 --> 06:36.242
That's why you can't move out of this crappy apartment.

06:36.702 --> 06:37.285
Look!

06:37.745 --> 06:39.318
Animation is not a hobby!

06:39.622 --> 06:40.413
It's a job!

06:41.999 --> 06:43.124
Sorry to bother you.

06:52.677 --> 06:54.636
I'm home!

06:55.054 --> 06:57.889
I almost drowned today.

06:59.058 --> 06:59.641
What?!

07:02.228 --> 07:03.937
Hey, what happened?!

07:04.939 --> 07:08.108
An animator guy saved me.

07:08.109 --> 07:09.943
He even kissed me.

07:10.653 --> 07:12.231
Sheesh, you...

07:12.571 --> 07:15.782
You know you can't swim, so be more careful!

07:15.866 --> 07:19.119
Doc, do you know what an animator is?

07:19.120 --> 07:23.790
An animator is an engineer who give life to images.

07:24.041 --> 07:25.750
Isn't it cool?

07:26.043 --> 07:27.392
Give me a break.

07:27.586 --> 07:28.420
Images are images.

07:28.963 --> 07:29.963
If they were living, then they'd be ghosts.

07:31.632 --> 07:35.135
If you have time to go see the
drawings at it he art museums,

07:35.136 --> 07:37.429
you need to watch TV and study anime!

07:41.533 --> 07:43.726
Ninki Production

07:51.360 --> 07:52.217
What's this?

07:52.570 --> 07:57.073
They are the frames for Roar, Solomon episode 28, cut 58.

07:57.325 --> 07:59.500
I can see that!

07:59.744 --> 08:02.412
I'm asking about this outrageous amount of images!

08:02.955 --> 08:06.791
But I was asked to work on the cut where Solomon runs.

08:07.251 --> 08:10.525
I see that you are a talented animator.

08:10.838 --> 08:13.632
But I can't make an-exception just for you.

08:14.050 --> 08:15.009
Director...

08:14.467 --> 08:15.807
He's right!

08:16.177 --> 08:21.264
Everyon is working hard to make
images move in a limited number of frames!

08:21.265 --> 08:24.103
And you drew so much just to make him run!

08:24.518 --> 08:27.341
I want to make Solomon move like he's alive!

08:27.605 --> 08:28.229
Director!

08:29.023 --> 08:32.317
Sorry, but I cannot use these frames.

08:34.695 --> 08:37.405
Animation is a collaborative work.

08:37.865 --> 08:40.075
It's not the work of a single man.

08:40.701 --> 08:44.412
I cannot allow such a selfish act.

08:44.997 --> 08:46.122
Please understand.

08:54.674 --> 08:55.924
Yo, Musashi.

08:57.426 --> 08:58.426
Kojiro-kun.

08:58.636 --> 09:01.721
Since I see it right there with you, it didn't pass, huh?

09:03.724 --> 09:06.434
That's why I told you, it's not a hobby.

09:07.728 --> 09:09.437
Don't waste your talent.

09:11.357 --> 09:14.109
It's a job, so you have to compromise.

09:14.860 --> 09:17.821
Why don't you relax a little?

09:18.531 --> 09:21.908
Sorry, but I have no intention of changing my views.

09:33.754 --> 09:34.379
What's wrong?!

09:35.089 --> 09:36.423
No, it's nothing.

09:55.486 --> 09:57.217
Relax?

09:57.447 --> 10:00.407
Solomon won't move like that!

10:00.575 --> 10:03.477
I want to move Solomon as much as possible!

10:03.828 --> 10:04.703
As if he's alive!

10:06.414 --> 10:07.915
Hello.

10:07.916 --> 10:09.541
I'm here again.

10:09.542 --> 10:10.334
Oh?

10:13.463 --> 10:14.838
What's the matter?

10:15.423 --> 10:16.798
Oh, you guys.

10:17.592 --> 10:20.636
When I finished, I took them to the producers...

10:21.137 --> 10:22.429
but they won't use them.

10:26.111 --> 10:28.393
They said I try too hard.

10:29.020 --> 10:32.492
I just want to draw a living animation.

10:34.901 --> 10:38.237
Maybe I'm not cut out for this job.

10:40.031 --> 10:41.198
That's not true!

10:44.327 --> 10:48.349
There's no way you're not cut out for
the job when you can draw so well!

10:48.623 --> 10:49.665
She's right!

10:49.666 --> 10:51.166
Please don't give up!

10:52.669 --> 10:55.254
I will try hard so I can swim.

10:56.714 --> 10:58.465
I won't give up either!

10:58.466 --> 11:01.593
So please don't say that you'll quit!

11:01.594 --> 11:02.594
Yeah!

11:02.595 --> 11:07.349
If I can swim, then you must become a great animator too!

11:21.364 --> 11:22.573
You're right.

11:25.618 --> 11:27.035
Fine.

11:27.036 --> 11:29.329
No use sulking here.

11:29.956 --> 11:30.664
Let's go.

11:30.665 --> 11:31.582
To where?

11:34.653 --> 11:35.319
To the pool!

11:35.393 --> 11:36.033
The pool!

11:41.009 --> 11:42.092
Yup, yup.

11:42.093 --> 11:44.720
You have to use your legs.

11:49.851 --> 11:50.851
Come on...

11:53.771 --> 11:55.939
Thank you, both of you.

11:59.027 --> 12:01.403
I'm grateful that you showed me.

12:04.908 --> 12:07.492
All I have is anime.

12:10.330 --> 12:14.416
I will save money, and make those
frames into an anime of my own some day.

12:14.417 --> 12:17.711
You two will be the first to see it when it's done.

12:18.212 --> 12:19.671
You swear?

12:19.672 --> 12:20.797
You promise?

12:31.267 --> 12:32.434
What's wrong?

12:32.435 --> 12:33.560
Musashi-san!

12:39.359 --> 12:40.984
Sharaku!

12:48.952 --> 12:50.911
Somebody!

13:01.381 --> 13:02.377
It's an acute case.

13:02.632 --> 13:03.548
Stomach cramp?

13:09.764 --> 13:11.431
Are you okay?

13:11.766 --> 13:13.517
Doc, there's trouble!

13:14.394 --> 13:16.478
He started rolling around in pain all of a sudden?

13:17.021 --> 13:18.272
Leave him to the ambulance.

13:18.773 --> 13:20.983
But would you come?

13:20.984 --> 13:24.987
You might be the only person who can save him.

13:25.363 --> 13:27.057
This is not an emergency center.

13:27.240 --> 13:29.241
I only see patients with appointments.

13:29.951 --> 13:32.703
If you've called for the ambulance, there's no room for me.

13:32.829 --> 13:37.583
The guy who's sick is the guy who saved me, Doc!

13:37.584 --> 13:38.375
Oh, yeah?

13:38.376 --> 13:42.504
That's a bummer that he got
sick before you could say thanks.

13:42.505 --> 13:44.172
That's not the point!

13:45.133 --> 13:46.813
Sorry, but I'm a doctor.

13:47.051 --> 13:48.010
Not a volunteer worker.

13:51.222 --> 13:55.100
Jeez, Doc!

14:12.785 --> 14:13.827
You're awake.

14:15.622 --> 14:17.831
Pinoco-chan, Sharaku-kun...

14:18.541 --> 14:19.541
Where am I?

14:19.542 --> 14:20.417
At a hospital.

14:20.835 --> 14:24.713
Don't you remember being
carried in here after you collapsed?

14:26.424 --> 14:29.551
Oh... yeah...

14:31.804 --> 14:33.972
I'm sick, right?

14:33.973 --> 14:35.515
I wonder if I can survive?

14:36.434 --> 14:39.063
It feels like I won't.

14:39.312 --> 14:40.938
What are you talking about?

14:40.939 --> 14:43.065
Of course you will.

14:43.066 --> 14:45.359
Yeah, you're fine!

14:45.902 --> 14:47.110
Promise...

14:48.488 --> 14:50.906
The promise that I will make a living anime...

14:51.699 --> 14:53.242
I might break it.

15:02.168 --> 15:03.794
He drowned in the pool, right?

15:04.254 --> 15:06.088
Then why do I have to go see him?

15:06.673 --> 15:08.257
No, Doc.

15:08.258 --> 15:10.821
He has a serious illness.

15:11.010 --> 15:14.012
Musashi-san is so depressed that he might die at this rate.

15:14.973 --> 15:16.515
He's in the hospital, right?

15:17.934 --> 15:21.395
Besides, who would pay for it if I operated on him?

15:23.064 --> 15:28.694
Well, it might be a different story
if he has something worth a lot.

15:31.781 --> 15:32.781
He does!

15:34.951 --> 15:37.202
He does, so please come with us!

15:43.251 --> 15:44.017
What are they?

15:44.252 --> 15:45.752
They are Musashi-san's anime frames.

15:47.171 --> 15:48.130
Anime frames?

15:48.965 --> 15:51.717
They might not be worth much yet,

15:51.718 --> 15:55.929
but if Musashi-san recovers, and continues to work hard,

15:55.930 --> 15:58.181
then they will be worth a lot eventually!

15:58.600 --> 16:00.351
Hey, hey, that's ridiculous...

15:59.934 --> 16:02.060
What he said is right.

16:04.939 --> 16:06.064
Kojiro-san!

16:09.444 --> 16:10.121
Who are you?

16:10.361 --> 16:12.070
I'm in the same profession as Musashi.

16:12.488 --> 16:14.364
I heard that Musashi was ill.

16:15.033 --> 16:15.699
And?

16:16.200 --> 16:16.992
I guarantee it.

16:17.493 --> 16:20.787
If he lives, he will accomplish something.

16:23.166 --> 16:27.878
In other words, losing him would
be a great blow to this industry.

16:29.339 --> 16:31.131
That's just convenient for you.

16:31.549 --> 16:32.883
Doc!

16:34.302 --> 16:35.382
Look at this picture!

16:35.382 --> 16:36.386
The man's picture!

16:40.683 --> 16:41.600
Look!

16:55.281 --> 17:00.535
Can't you see that it would be
wonderful if these pictures moved?

17:17.637 --> 17:19.096
Well, I guess I can't help it.

17:20.056 --> 17:22.683
However, there is one condition.

17:32.277 --> 17:33.569
We're commencing the operation.

17:44.581 --> 17:45.372
Probe.

17:47.083 --> 17:47.791
Gauze.

18:04.601 --> 18:06.184
This is the peritoneum type.

18:06.728 --> 18:08.186
And it has spread, too.

18:09.689 --> 18:11.189
This will take a while.

18:14.736 --> 18:19.072
It'd probably be impossible to save
him with the skill level of this hospital.

18:25.705 --> 18:27.164
But I can.

18:40.216 --> 18:42.056
Operation in progress

18:44.390 --> 18:45.140
Doc!

18:46.476 --> 18:47.517
The operation was successful.

18:47.518 --> 18:48.310
Really?

18:48.311 --> 18:49.436
Yeah!

18:49.437 --> 18:53.941
But, just as you said, the patient is mentally exhausted.

18:56.694 --> 19:00.405
But they should be making the medicine for it now.

19:15.838 --> 19:17.005
<i>Where am I?</i>

19:18.758 --> 19:20.092
<i>I can't see anything.</i>

19:28.726 --> 19:29.726
<i>I'm scared.</i>

19:30.186 --> 19:31.353
<i>Am I...</i>

19:31.354 --> 19:33.021
<i>Am I done for already?</i>

19:44.200 --> 19:45.492
<i>What is that glow?</i>

19:52.083 --> 19:53.458
<i>Solomon!</i>

19:54.627 --> 19:55.335
<i>Solomon!</i>

20:01.676 --> 20:03.302
<i>Solomon! Wait!</i>

20:16.524 --> 20:19.610
<i>Solomon! Don't go!</i>

20:20.194 --> 20:22.863
<i>Solomon!</i>

20:30.496 --> 20:31.580
It was a dream.

20:42.216 --> 20:43.091
Solomon!

20:53.728 --> 20:55.062
Those are my frames!

20:55.480 --> 20:57.189
No, they are not.

20:58.816 --> 21:02.110
I took those frames as the fee for your operation.

21:02.987 --> 21:04.529
When was it completed?

21:05.365 --> 21:08.575
The guy in the same profession, Kojiro was his name?

21:09.202 --> 21:11.745
I asked him, and he completed it.

21:15.750 --> 21:18.043
Look, it's really well-made.

21:18.461 --> 21:19.753
It's as if he's alive.

21:20.630 --> 21:22.714
Kojiro-kun...

21:24.676 --> 21:27.302
Now that the lion is moving around, so lively,

21:27.804 --> 21:29.949
what good would it be for the creator to die?

21:30.431 --> 21:31.056
Eh?

21:33.893 --> 21:36.728
Musashi, come back soon.

21:36.813 --> 21:38.772
Everyone is waiting for you.

21:52.870 --> 21:57.207
Now, when will these pieces of papers turns into treasure?

22:07.080 --> 22:19.035
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.080 --> 22:19.035
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.153 --> 22:24.152
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.153 --> 22:24.152
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.721 --> 22:31.190
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.721 --> 22:31.190
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.734 --> 22:37.192
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.734 --> 22:37.192
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.796 --> 22:40.281
being heated up by you,

22:37.796 --> 22:40.281
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.490 --> 22:48.267
so much that I change color

22:40.490 --> 22:48.267
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.352 --> 23:00.121
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.352 --> 23:00.121
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.329 --> 23:12.060
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.329 --> 23:12.060
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.300 --> 23:23.651
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.300 --> 23:23.651
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.837 --> 23:28.758
I couldn't be happier

23:23.837 --> 23:28.758
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.986 --> 23:33.920
How does it taste?

23:28.986 --> 23:33.919
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.058 --> 24:15.040
The Fabricated Wedding

23:45.119 --> 23:50.216
I will marry the first man who enters this room.

23:50.338 --> 23:52.322
She won't last long!

23:52.345 --> 23:53.385
I understand.

23:53.525 --> 23:57.493
I think she's putting all of her hope for life in the wedding.

23:57.673 --> 24:02.966
I intend to finish the operation while
the anesthetic called hope is still in effect.

24:03.230 --> 24:04.230
Not yet?

24:04.513 --> 24:05.987
Michiru-chan is serious!

24:08.180 --> 24:11.147
Your wedding partner is me, Pinoco.

24:11.586 --> 24:14.199
Next Karte - The Fabricated Wedding.

24:16.106 --> 24:17.648
Karte NG...

24:18.650 --> 24:20.192
What's wrong?

24:20.193 --> 24:21.318
Musashi-san!

24:23.287 --> 24:24.453
It peeled off.
